From 6760578713e498725c5298a9b9a71d6ebc9e8f1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Che Haijun <chehaijun@ChedeMacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:50:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(codebook): hierarchical codebook with code-level
 maintenance

Projects move to schema v2. A code gains parent_id, memo, inclusion,
exclusion, anchor_examples, status and order; a document gains attributes.
migrate() upgrades v1 projects in place on first read, so existing codebooks,
codings and character offsets are preserved.

New operations: rename, redefine, recolour, re-parent, merge and delete a code.
The code tree is validated on every write (no self-parent, no missing parent,
no cycles). Merging collapses codings that would duplicate the target.

The sidebar renders the codebook as a tree with rolled-up counts and collapsible
branches, and the codings CSV gains a code_path column.
